    {
      "id": "S-LANA",
      "file": "research/round2-source-cache/LANA-interim-report-2026-07.txt",
      "sha256": "5fc6185d6642e70ba58c6ce637ef6e0448e2761b9d57b5e40545aea3d6ee040e",
      "bytes": 144233,
      "lines_total": 2341,
      "role": "primary formulation of (9-1)",
      "citations": [
        {
          "locator": "L1433-L1437",
          "page": "p.31",
          "topic": "(Ind3) is the root of the existential: only an adelic measurable subset is known, so all such subsets must be considered"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L1688-L1692",
          "page": "p.36",
          "topic": "Step 8: possible regions LGP·U for U ranging over suitable subsets of VC(I) - a family, not a fixed value"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L2060-L2061",
          "page": "p.44",
          "topic": "9.1 'We start with a BPS' - the input is fixed before any choice"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L2062-L2067",
          "page": "p.44",
          "topic": "9.1(a) Step 1 'Choose an isomorphism between the given BPS and the Theta-pilot BPS'"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L2117-L2120",
          "page": "p.45",
          "topic": "9.2 'after fixing an isomorphism between a given BPS and the Theta-BPS'"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L2123-L2132",
          "page": "p.46",
          "topic": "9.2 'Once we fix S subset VC(I_v) ... the isomorphism eta^anab_S : R_val -> R_ss ... depends on S'"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L2126",
          "page": "p.46",
          "topic": "R_ss defined as adelic measurable T / ~ with equal volume"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L2133-L2136",
          "page": "p.46",
          "topic": "eta_q exists on the fixed q-side input; pilot = class of {q_v O_v}"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L2138-L2141",
          "page": "p.46",
          "topic": "THE (9-1): 'there exists some suitable S such that eta_q = eta^anab_S .(9-1)'"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L2236-L2239",
          "page": "p.48",
          "topic": "the comparison is of the two constructions before computing degrees"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L2265-L2267",
          "page": "p.49",
          "topic": "Ind1/Ind2 'create ambiguities in the choice of the set S in (9-1)' - they enlarge the exists, not the reals"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L2274-L2282",
          "page": "p.49",
          "topic": "status: '(9-1) which is not manifestly false. However, we, the LANA project, do not have a proof of (9-1) at this time'"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "S-IUT3",
      "file": "research/round2-source-cache/iut-III-official-retrieved-2026-10-16.txt",
      "sha256": "70a618ada5e5039b84283c21fc1b947db9dced559d46ecb2786e05ae6164b715",
      "bytes": 570037,
      "lines_total": 11854,
      "role": "the source the S-form is a reconstruction of: Corollary 3.12 and Step (xi)",
      "citations": [
        {
          "locator": "L890-L908",
          "page": "p.16",
          "topic": "-|log(q)| is the log-volume of the q-pilot object; -|log(Theta)| is that of the holomorphic hull of the union of the possible images"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L9596-L9603",
          "page": "p.156",
          "topic": "(Ind3): 'as one varies m in Z, the isomorphisms of (a) are upper semi-compatible' - one-sided inclusions/surjections"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L10498-L10528",
          "page": "p.173-174",
          "topic": "Corollary 3.12 statement: hull of the union of the possible images; subject to (Ind1),(Ind2),(Ind3); conclusion -|log(Theta)| >= -|log(q)|"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L10506-L10513",
          "page": "p.173-174",
          "topic": "measured object = holomorphic hull of the UNION of the possible images (a sup, hence one-sided)"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L10549-L10577",
          "page": "p.174",
          "topic": "n,circ U = the collection of subsets; n,circ U = the holomorphic hulls of them"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L10965-L10981",
          "page": "p.182",
          "topic": "Step (xi): ('some' algorithm) that transforms input data into output data and satisfies (IPL), (SHE)"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L11007-L11047",
          "page": "p.183",
          "topic": "(xi-d) collection of possibilities of output data in the hull; R_{<=-|log(Theta)|} vs the fixed -|log(q)|"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L11048-L11072",
          "page": "p.183-184",
          "topic": "(xi-e) 'the relationship ... between the pilot-object log-volume -|log(q)| and the input data' is fixed by the 1-column structure"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L11073-L11083",
          "page": "p.184",
          "topic": "(xi-f) THE QUANTIFIER: 'The inclusion -|log(q)| in R_{<=-|log(Theta)|}, hence also the inequality ... then follows formally' - membership, with 'perhaps only up to some sort of approximation'"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L11084-L11088",
          "page": "p.184",
          "topic": "(xi-g) 'two tautologically equivalent ways to compute the log-volume of the q-pilot object at (1,0)'"
        },
        {
          "locator": "L9720-L9724",
          "page": "p.157-158",
          "topic": "Theorem 3.11 compatibility 'up to the indeterminacies (Ind1), (Ind2), (Ind3)'"
        }
      ]
    },
